Patients in the highest tertile of TyG index had 3.09-fold higher risk for TA/IF compared with those in the lowest tertile. The TyG index was independently and positively associated with the risk of TA/IF (odds ratio [OR]:3.830, 95% confidence interval [CI] 2.578-5.691; p < 0.001). SBP was found to mediate the association between TyG index and TA/IF, with a proportion mediated of 20.7% observed in the highest TyG index tertile (OR [indirect association]: 1.319, 95% CI: 1.118-1.558). The developed predictive nomogram model incorporated SBP, estimated glomerular filtration rate, TyG index, high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and proteinuria; it demonstrated good predictive performance with strong discrimination (area under the curve: 0.864;

